@domain:repository-scanning @area:skipped-files @from:gradebook-code/collection
Feature: Leaving generated and test files out of the code score
  Lets a maintainer trust that the code score describes only the code people write and maintain, not generated output or the test suite.

  Background:
    Given a repository the operator wants to grade with gradebook-code

  @id:gradebook-code.repository-scanning.skipped-files.006 @rule:code.scanning.generated-files-skipped-and-counted @verified @source:gradebook-code/gradebook_code/collection.py#_sources @test:gradebook-code/tests/test_gradebook_code.py#test_generated_files_are_excluded_from_the_score @test:gradebook-code/tests/test_gradebook_code.py#test_generated_files_are_recognised
  Scenario Outline: Generated and minified files are skipped and the number skipped is reported
    Given the repository holds the hand-written file "src/real.py"
    And the repository holds the file "<generated_file>" that <why_generated>
    When the operator grades the repository
    Then only 1 source file is scored
    And the report says 1 generated file was skipped
    And nothing in "<generated_file>" counts towards any finding or dimension

    Examples:
      | generated_file | why_generated                                               |
      | src/api_pb2.py | is a protobuf output by name                                |
      | web/app.min.js | is minified by name                                         |
      | pkg/wire.go    | starts with "Code generated by protoc. DO NOT EDIT."        |
      | web/bundle.js  | has a line longer than 500 characters in its first 50 lines |

  @id:gradebook-code.repository-scanning.skipped-files.007 @rule:code.scanning.test-files-not-scored @verified @source:gradebook-code/gradebook_code/collection.py#_sources @test:gradebook-code/tests/test_gradebook_code.py#test_only_source_files_are_counted @test:gradebook-code/tests/test_gradebook_code.py#test_test_files_are_excluded
  Scenario Outline: Test files are not part of the code score
    Given the repository holds the source file "src/a.py" with one function
    And the repository holds the test file "<test_file>"
    When the operator grades the repository
    Then only 1 source file is scored
    And only 1 function is counted

    Examples:
      | test_file          |
      | tests/test_a.py    |
      | src/a.spec.ts      |
      | pkg/a_test.go      |
      | spec/a_spec.rb     |
      | src/__tests__/a.js |
